# paradigmxyz/reth#23603 "fix(db): use sync=true for rocksdb WriteOptions"
# (3a136fc, in the pinned reth). Tempo d3f3b28f runs reth's storage v2
# (`--storage.v2` defaults to true at 42fa3c5), which keeps
# TransactionHashNumbers and the account/storage history indices in RocksDB
# while blocks, changesets and checkpoints are in MDBX and static files.
# Before the fix, RocksDB commits left their WAL writes un-synced while MDBX
# commits were fsync'd: a machine crash could keep a block in MDBX/static
# files whose tx-hash lookups and history entries RocksDB had lost (startup
# healing only prunes RocksDB when it is ahead). A process kill keeps the page
# cache, so only storage_faults' machine crashes can reach it.
#
# The fix no longer reverts cleanly (later commits added flush_wal paths), so
# the patch sets synced_write_options() back to sync=false. Live-sync
# persistence never calls flush_wal (only the pipeline stages and Drop do).
RETH_PATCH=reth-23603.patch
VARIANT=default
# Machine crashes only: the bug needs un-synced RocksDB writes lost, which
# every crash does; torn writes add nothing to it.
CAMPAIGN_ARGS="--workload-arg storage_faults=true --workload-arg storage_fault_kinds=crash"
EXPECT=E11/
